R2 Integration Hardening — Checklist

## 1. Sanitize uploaded filename

- [ ] Strip path components
- [ ] Replace `/` and `\` with `_`
- [ ] Allow only `[a-zA-Z0-9._-]`
- [ ] Enforce allowed extensions: `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.webp`
- [ ] Implement in: `core_operations/src/handlers/product_images/get_presigned_upload_url.rs`

## 2. Validate Content-Type and enforce file size limit

- [ ] Validate MIME type against an allowlist
- [ ] Add max upload size validation
- [ ] Optionally store expected size for later verification
- [ ] Update: `GetPresignedUploadUrlRequest` (proto) and `get_presigned_upload_url.rs`

## 3. Verify object exists before DB insert

- [ ] Add `head_object()` (or equivalent) check before inserting DB record
- [ ] Validate that the object exists in R2
- [ ] Store file size in DB
- [ ] Implement in: `confirm_image_upload.rs`

## 4. Remove or properly implement thumbnail logic

- [ ] Decide on strategy:
  - [ ] Remove thumbnail logic completely, **or**
  - [ ] Implement background thumbnail generation, **or**
  - [ ] Migrate to Cloudflare Images

## 5. Add Cache-Control headers

- [ ] Use immutable object naming (UUID-based keys)
- [ ] Set `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`
- [ ] Ensure upload client sends/sets required headers

## 6. Improve R2 client configuration

- [ ] Enable `force_path_style(true)` if required by the endpoint
- [ ] Add a startup connectivity test to R2 (fail fast if unreachable)

## 7. Enforce required R2 environment variables at startup

- [ ] Validate presence of:
  - [ ] `R2_ACCOUNT_ID`
  - [ ] `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`
  - [ ] `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`
  - [ ] `R2_BUCKET_NAME`
  - [ ] `R2_PUBLIC_URL`
- [ ] Fail fast on missing/invalid configuration

## 8. Remove dead code around R2

- [ ] Remove unused imports
- [ ] Delete placeholder / unused functions
- [ ] Ensure `cargo clippy` passes cleanly

## 9. Add DB constraints for product images

- [ ] Add index on `(product_id, display_order)`
- [ ] Add unique constraint on `(product_id, cdn_path)`
- [ ] Enforce a single primary image per product (if applicable)

## 10. Implement orphan cleanup strategy

- [ ] Create a cleanup job for unconfirmed uploads
- [ ] Delete unconfirmed objects older than N hours, **or**
- [ ] Track pending uploads with expiration and clean them up

## 11. Logging & observability

- [ ] Log presigned URL generation (success/failure + key metadata)
- [ ] Log confirm-upload success/failure with enough context
- [ ] Add metrics for upload failures and cleanup actions

## 12. Security review

- [ ] Ensure the R2 bucket is **not** public write
- [ ] Use minimal-privilege R2 API tokens/keys
- [ ] Document and schedule periodic rotation of access keys

## End goal

Secure, validated, cache-optimized, and production-safe R2 integration.
